# 🧭 Bada Project Rules (v1.3)
**Author:** Junseo Park
**Copyright:** © 2025 Studio_bada.
**Target:** All projects under Studio_bada, including divetobada.com, Chartroom, Workflow, etc.

---

## 1. Non-Negotiable Rules
1. The model must **never** alter or propose code without instruction.
2. Execution is allowed **only after approval** following a clear proposal.
3. Maintain the current state of all existing functions and components unless explicitly told otherwise.
4. Any new feature must **not break existing ones** under any circumstances.

---

## 2. Technical Stack Consistency
| Component | Technology |
|------------|-------------|
| **Language** | TypeScript (JS) |
| **Framework** | Next.js |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL |
| **ORM** | Prisma |
| **Styling** | Tailwind CSS *(optional)* |
| **Editor** | Tiptap |
| **Icons** | lucide-icon *(use only when absolutely necessary)* |
| **Auth** | Lucia |
| **File Storage** | Vercel Blob |
| **Validation** | Zod |

> These technologies define the official structure of Studio_bada projects.
> All changes or replacements require prior approval from Junseo.
> Consistency and efficiency must always be prioritized.

---

## 3. Design Policy
- Every Studio_bada product must follow the **divetobada.com visual framework**.
- Maintain the same typography, spacing, hierarchy, and component patterns.
- **Icons should be avoided** whenever possible.
- UI or animation changes must be reviewed before implementation.
- No arbitrary or aesthetic-only edits are allowed.

---

## 4. Version Control & Data Management
- Never execute `git clean -fdx`.
- Always run `git clean -n` first if absolutely required.
- Keep backup folders (`backups/`) outside the project directory or in cloud storage.
- Never apply migrations to the production database.
  - All experiments must use a **local or sandboxed database** only.

---

## 5. Learning from Past Failures
- Past mistakes recorded in reflection logs (`worklog_YYYY-MM-DD.md`) are considered **binding lessons**.
- The model should use those reflections to prevent recurrence,
  but must **not replicate failed structures or temporary fixes**.
- Reference: *"작업복기_2025-10-07.md" (Oct 7, 2025)* contains critical lessons regarding layout mismanagement, honesty in reporting, and safe git practices.
  These principles are integrated into this document.

---

## 6. Deployment & Domain Management

### Vercel 배포 도메인 연결 문제
- **문제**: GitHub 푸시 후 자동 배포가 성공해도 `www.divetobada.com`에 변경사항이 자동 반영되지 않을 수 있음
- **해결 방법**: 최신 Production 배포를 찾아 도메인에 수동으로 연결해야 함
  ```bash
  # 1. 최신 Production 배포 확인
  npx vercel ls bada5-0 | grep "Production" | head -1
  
  # 2. 최신 배포를 도메인에 연결
  LATEST_DEPLOY=$(npx vercel ls bada5-0 | grep "Production" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}')
  npx vercel alias set $LATEST_DEPLOY www.divetobada.com
  npx vercel alias set $LATEST_DEPLOY divetobada.com
  ```
- **참고**: `bada5-0` 프로젝트에 도메인이 연결되어 있음

---

## 7. Enforcement and Compliance
- This rule set is **mandatory**, not advisory.
- Violations may result in loss of trust or project damage and are treated as critical incidents.
- Every task must end with:
  > "This work complies with the project rules and Studio_bada's copyright and design integrity standards."